    "body": "Premise note (maintainer decision on PR #2997, 2026-11-20): the 3+2 first-traverse law takes the unknown start at the Z travel top (the tool-change height), the same premise as the upright law. It does not cover a program that starts with the tool low near the table or the work (for example after a manual jog). The work on this issue uses the same premise, and it states this limit in its decision file.",
